AUDIO: 'Want to try some new creative shots? &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; In this video, we\'ll walk you through four creative shooting modes to help you capture stunning high-quality shots with ease. Mode selection. From the shooting mode page, you can choose classic creative modes such'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] as panorama, time lapse, and time shift. Tap the icon in the top right corner to enter the creative library and explore new effects such as barrel roll and slow-mo live.'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '360 panorama. This allows you to capture [music] an immersive 360 shot and unlock the tiny planet effect. Swipe left or right on the center'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] of the screen and select panorama. Then choose 360. The gimbal will rotate and capture 19 images to create a 360 image of its surroundings. You can set a timer by swiping up from'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the bottom of the screen. Time lapse. If you want to create atmospheric time lapse footage, [music] Luna Ultra offers two modes to create with. Time lapse. For shooting from a fixed'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'position, time lapse takes photos at regular intervals and then stitches them together to make a video. This mode is ideal for capturing sunrises [music] and busy city scenes.'

[01:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Time shift. For shooting while moving, time shift records continuous video and speeds [music] it up. Barrel roll.'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Want a cinematic sci-fi look? In rotation shot mode, the camera automatically rotates while filming to create surreal dream-like visuals. Two grip styles are available, vertical'

[01:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and [music] horizontal. Tap the settings icon in the bottom right corner to switch between them. By default, the camera is set to vertical grip, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; which supports up to 90° rotation. For wider rotational movement, switch to'

[01:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'horizontal grip for up to 180° In the settings, [music] you can also adjust the rotation speed and direction to customize your shooting. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[02:05] [scene:talk]
